{
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_intro": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "title": "Wind Compass",
      "description": "Live wind & weather compass for Dashboard Studio",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "A self-contained, zero-setup compass visualization — pick a city and go, no index, inputs, or search data required. Three looks are shown below: a dark theme, a light theme, and a weather-only view with the dial hidden. Prefer your own data instead? See **How it works** right below. Live-mode weather data via [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/), used under [CC BY 4.0](https://open-meteo.com/en/license) — full attribution at the bottom of this dashboard.",
        "backgroundColor": "#171a21"
      }
    },
    "viz_howitworks_live": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "title": "Live mode",
      "description": "Powered by Open-Meteo",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "- Set a **City** (required) and **Country** (optional — disambiguates same-named cities) under the panel's **Data source** options.\n- Your browser calls Open-Meteo's free [geocoding](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/geocoding-api) API to resolve the city to coordinates, then its [forecast](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs) API for current wind, temperature, and weather condition.\n- No Splunk index, data input, or search is required — the panel renders real data immediately after you set a city.\n- Auto-refreshes on your configured interval (default 300s, minimum 60s).\n- No API key, and no Splunk data is ever sent to Open-Meteo — see Attribution at the bottom of this dashboard.",
        "backgroundColor": "#13202c"
      }
    },
    "viz_howitworks_search": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "title": "Search mode",
      "description": "Bring your own data",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "- Set **Data source → Mode** to **Search**, then bind a search returning one row to the panel.\n- Required fields: wind **direction** (0–360°, meteorological convention — direction the wind comes from) and wind **speed**, both numeric.\n- Optional fields: location, country, temperature, wind gusts, weather code, and is-day — map field names under **Search: field mapping**.\n- Default field names match Open-Meteo's own schema (`wind_direction_10m`, `wind_speed_10m`, `temperature_2m`, …), but any numeric fields work.",
        "backgroundColor": "#17241c"
      }
    },
